        "original_id": "364aa888-fa5d-58a2-aa76-05c2c76faea4",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Pascoe St Leger Grenfell\n- Organizations: South Australian Church Society, Trinity City\n- Places: North Terrace, Adelaide, Holy Trinity Church, Adelaide\n- Topics: church construction, Sunday gatherings\n\nFacts:\n- Pascoe St Leger Grenfell was a valued committee member of the South Australian Church Society.\n- Pascoe St Leger Grenfell donated an acre of land on North Terrace in Adelaide for the construction of Holy Trinity Church.\n- Holy Trinity Church was one of the first churches built in the city of Adelaide and in the colony.\n- Trinity City holds four gatherings each Sunday at the North Terrace location.\n- Trinity City also holds various other meetings throughout the week at the North Terrace location.",
